{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION to prior grounding comment: pydantic-ai 1.107.2 DOES expose a public InstrumentedModel — verified in-env: pydantic_ai.models.instrumented.InstrumentedModel (a WrapperModel subclass) and InstrumentationSettings both import. My earlier 'no public InstrumentedModel' claim was wrong (it is not in the top-level pydantic_ai namespace but IS a documented public API under .models.instrumented). Plan v3 now REUSES InstrumentedModel/WrapperModel for candidate spans rather than a bespoke tracer (resolves T1).\n\nAlso resolved: (a) prerequisite-consistency vs S2 — S4 makes NO _pai_structured change; it only OBSERVES the S2-preserved bug-895c native->prompted fallback (S2 AC-7). Both the native and prompted agent.run route through the same wrapped candidates, so the downgrade is legible as native-span raised then prompted-span returned with zero control-flow change. Dropped structured_run.py from scope/file_impact; removed all 'adds a second Agent run by design' language. (b) T8 sanitization — raised-reason text now routed through the existing rebar.llm.failure.sanitize_diagnostic allowlist. (c) T8/T5b tracing-ON failure — instrumentation is best-effort: span/exporter errors are swallowed at the wrapper boundary so result/usage/exception are identical to tracing-off, pinned by a new tracing-ON span-failure test. (d) P6 — bundled ACs split into 8 atomic criteria."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786962524203879001,"uuid":"5af0cbd2-c746-4d13-bd15-983696580f41"}